" IdeaVim configuration
" Stowed from ~/.dotfiles/ideavim/.ideavimrc (linked as ~/.ideavimrc)
source ~/.lazy-idea/lazy-idea.vim

" Keep NERDTree working in the Project tool window when no editor is open.
"
" With no editor open, IdeaVim's OutsideEditorKeyDispatcher registers every
" normal-mode mapping that runs a bare <Action>(...) on the focused component.
" In the Project View that component is the tree itself. IntelliJ only consults
" the nearest component that has custom actions, so that registration shadows
" the NERDTree dispatcher, which is registered on the Project View's parent
" component. h/j/k/l then fall through to the tree and start Speed Search
" instead of navigating.
"
" OutsideEditorKeyDispatcher only exists to make <Action>(...) mappings usable
" with no editor open. Turning it off restores NERDTree; those mappings keep
" working normally from an editor buffer.
set noideaoutsideeditor

" Re-arm NERDTree if its keys ever stop working, e.g. after the Project View
" component is rebuilt. Run it from an editor buffer.
nnoremap <silent> <leader>nR :set noNERDTree<CR>:set NERDTree<CR>
